The stack-depth failure comes from chaining: 4 chained jobs × (test frame + trigger frame) exceeds the chained-job stack depth of 5 in test context. For the stated volumes (1 at a time, or up to 200 per batch) chaining is never needed — the trigger can enqueue at most 2 jobs of 100 callouts each, so I split into jobs **at enqueue time** and keep the chain depth at 2. The 100-callout platform limit per job is still respected.

